  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tahoe. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tahoe (also known as Wichita Hold'em) is a community card poker game similar to Texas Hold'em and Pineapple. Players receive three hole cards (sometimes two, but usually three in the Tahoe variant) and share five community cards. The key restriction is that players may use zero, one, or two of their hole cards to form a handâ€”never all three. It is often played High-Low Split.",
    objective: 'Win the pot with the best 5-card hand. (Often High-Low split).',
    gameplay: '1. Deal 3 hole cards. 2. Pre-flop betting. 3. Flop (3 cards). 4. Betting. 5. Turn (1 card). 6. Betting. 7. River (1 card). 8. Betting. 9. Showdown. Restriction: Use 0, 1, or 2 hole cards. You cannot use all 3. (Unlike Omaha where you must use 2, or Pineapple where you discard one).',
